<title>USA: NGC Corp Q1 shr down.</title>
<headline>NGC Corp Q1 shr down.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>NGC CORPORATION</p>
<p>		    (In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>						     Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							   March 31,</p>
<p>						     1997	     1996</p>
<p> Operating Revenues		  $   3,272,080  $   1,647,123</p>
<p> Operating Income			     15,800	   53,636</p>
<p> Interest Expense			   (14,624)	 (10,653)</p>
<p>Equity in Earnings of Unconsolidated</p>
<p>  Affiliates				    13,386	    4,510</p>
<p> Other Income and (Deductions), Net   (10,133)	    (872)</p>
<p> Income Before Income Taxes		  4,429	   46,621</p>
<p>Provision for (Benefit from) Income Taxes</p>
<p>						     (185)	   16,293</p>
<p> Net Income					4,614	   30,328</p>
<p>Earnings Per Share of Common Stock and</p>
<p>  Common Stock Equivalents Outstanding    0.03	     0.26</p>
<p>Average Shares of Common Stock and Equivalents</p>
<p> Outstanding				   167,813	  118,923</p>
<p>NOTE:  The 1997 first quarter results include previously announced charges totaling $20.6 million, $13.0 million after tax, or $0.08 per share, related to the company's natural gas liquids business; a $2.7 million pretax, $1.7 million after tax, or $0.01 per share charge to reduce the company's crude oil inventories to market prices, and a gain of $3.4 million, $2.2 million after tax, or $0.01 per share, from the sale of its Mont Belvieu fractionation unit.  The company also has established a reserve related to its investment in a storage project of $15.0 million, $9.5 million after tax, or $.05 per share. Excluding the charges and gain, NGC's net income for the first quarter of 1997 was $26.6 million, or $0.16 per share.</p>
